00:08:33.409 --> 00:08:34.576
GAURAV AGGARWAL: Definitely.

00:08:34.576 --> 00:08:37.429
So I just want to highlight,
why do we need each component?

00:08:37.429 --> 00:08:40.440
Why can't we just, you know, get
data from point of the system,

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.030
and that should be enough?

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.310
So with point is the system,
you get historical data.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:47.570
So we understand that launch
is going to be a busy time,

00:08:47.570 --> 00:08:49.650
Friday evenings are a busy time.

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.410
But there are these
anomalous events,

00:08:51.410 --> 00:08:52.827
like when you're
in a stadium, you

00:08:52.827 --> 00:08:54.910
don't know when the game
is going to be scheduled.

00:08:54.910 --> 00:08:56.870
It can be on the weekend,
but time can vary.

00:08:56.870 --> 00:09:00.050
If you're a bar in front of
the stadium, you will have,

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:02.370
once the game is over,
a lot of people come in.

00:09:02.370 --> 00:09:04.670
And so you need to
model this thing.

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:07.070
And we cannot ignore these
spikes because we are

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:10.220
in the business of giving
the right wait time most

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:11.113
of the time.

00:09:11.113 --> 00:09:13.530
Although we can just say, 10
minutes wait time on average,

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:14.460
and you should be happy.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:15.752
That's not how it works for us.

00:09:15.752 --> 00:09:17.030
We need to be very accurate.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:20.330
That's what we need to do to
figure out wait time on ground,

00:09:20.330 --> 00:09:21.493
how many people are there?

00:09:21.493 --> 00:09:22.910
And we have tried
computer vision.

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:25.850
We use state of the art
[INAUDIBLE] computer models.

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:28.350
And we wanted to be able
to do better than that.

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:29.600
But the privacy was a concern.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.810
So we ended up using a very
proprietary technology,

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:37.092
where it's like a size
of, like, an iPhone,

00:09:37.092 --> 00:09:39.050
where we have this thing
where you can plug in.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.600
It detects how many people
are in the vicinity.

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:43.040
And it can make
a differentiation

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.540
in terms of how
many of these people

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.480
