again, because we

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:07.540
were on AWS back then.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:10.790
But are currently
being migrated to DCP4

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:12.538
for our modeling purposes.

00:10:12.538 --> 00:10:14.830
FILLIPO MADELLA: So you are
leveraging machine learning

00:10:14.830 --> 00:10:17.908
models to create a lot of these
priority cues and predictions.

00:10:17.908 --> 00:10:19.450
So could you expand
a little bit more

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:22.523
on how you designed
this ML pipeline?

00:10:22.523 --> 00:10:23.440
GAURAV AGGARWAL: Sure.

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.050
So we have these
small IT devices,

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:29.710
which gathers data and
sends this anonymous data

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.100
to our services.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.530
So two types of data
sets are sent to us.

00:10:33.530 --> 00:10:36.310
One type of data set is
the real-time, that kind of

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:37.630
feeds into our system.

00:10:37.630 --> 00:10:41.802
And it is directly sent out to
our services running in GKE.

00:10:41.802 --> 00:10:44.260
So it kind of gives an idea,
aggregated, of how many people

